MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A14, D679/D680: when the bridge AND the receiver are both „not of this field"
by their own data, a request only waits for a no. closedRoute.ts reads both
pre-matches for the requester's goal before the request is made.

HELD (D44): the model line is NIGHT_QUESTIONS AO, waiting for Misho's yes.
With CLOSED_ROUTE_ON = false nothing is refused; the request goes as before
and one [closed-route] log line says what would have been stopped, so the
morning has evidence of how often it bites. Anything unknown (no goal, no
receiver phone, a failed read) counts as open — a request is never stopped
on a guess. Direct requests are never checked.

